---
/**
 * Reference — the five skills, the four rules, and what the gate actually
 * checks.
 *
 * Everything on this page that repeats is data. The skills and the audit rules
 * are the same shape rendered by the same row component, which is the point:
 * two lists that look alike are one component with different data, not two
 * components waiting to drift.
 */
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro'
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro'
import Section from '../components/Section.astro'
import DefinitionRow from '../components/DefinitionRow.astro'
import RoleBadge from '../components/RoleBadge.astro'
import RichText from '../components/RichText.astro'
import Text from '../components/ui/Text.astro'
import Code from '../components/ui/Code.astro'
import CodeBlock from '../components/ui/CodeBlock.astro'
import Card from '../components/ui/Card.astro'
import { skills } from '../fixtures/skills'
import { auditRules } from '../fixtures/audit-rules'

const HOUSE_RULES = [
  'Every colour, size, radius and shadow comes from the token file. There is one per project.',
  'A value used twice is a token. A shape used twice is a component.',
  'Every screen answers for its four states: ready, empty, loading, error.',
  'The audit is blocking. A waiver needs a reason written on the line above it.',
]

const AUDIT_OUTPUT = `  arbitrary-scale - 135 in 43 places
  An arbitrary value on a scale property. It is a scale step nobody declared.
   27 x  text-[13px]        components/AppSidebarItem.astro:34 +26
   14 x  rounded-[8px]      components/AppSidebarItem.astro:34 +13
  -> Add it to the theme scale, then use the named step.`

const WAIVER = `<!-- ui-audit-allow: inline-style — third-party embed, the vendor sets the style -->`
---

<Page
  title="Reference — cairn"
  description="The five cairn skills, the four composition rules, and the ten rules the gate intercepts."
>
  <PageIntro
    title="Reference"
    lead="Five skills. Two are read by both roles, and one of those is what holds the rest together."
  />

  <div class="mt-16 space-y-16">
    <Section title="The five skills">
      <dl class="border-t border-rule">
        {
          skills.map((skill) => (
            <DefinitionRow
              term={skill.name}
              emphasis={skill.readBy === 'both' ? 'strong' : 'default'}
            >
              <RoleBadge slot="aside" role={skill.readBy} />
              {skill.when}
            </DefinitionRow>
          ))
        }
      </dl>

      <Text variant="note" class="mt-6 max-w-2xl">
        <Code>ui-composition</Code> is shared deliberately. Two copies of one law would drift within
        a month, and drifting rules are the problem this system exists to solve.
      </Text>
    </Section>

    <Section title="The rules, in four lines">
      <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        {
          HOUSE_RULES.map((rule, index) => (
            <Card elevation="flat">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide text-primary">
                {String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
              </span>
              <Text variant="lead" class="mt-3 font-display">
                {rule}
              </Text>
            </Card>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section title="What the gate checks">
      <Text class="max-w-2xl">
        The check has no opinion about beauty. It sees only what is mechanical — and that is
        already enough.
      </Text>

      <dl class="mt-8 border-t border-rule">
        {
          auditRules.map((rule) => (
            <DefinitionRow term={rule.id}>
              <RichText copy={rule.catches} />
            </DefinitionRow>
          ))
        }
      </dl>

      <CodeBlock class="mt-8" label="sample output" code={AUDIT_OUTPUT} />

      <Text variant="note" class="mt-6 max-w-2xl">
        135 findings are really 43 decisions. The report groups them on purpose: a long list gets
        ignored, forty choices get made in an afternoon.
      </Text>
    </Section>

    <Section title="When a rule is wrong">
      <Text class="max-w-2xl">
        Sooner or later one will be. Take the waiver, write the reason on the line above it, and
        record it in the project contract. If the same waiver is taken a third time, the rule is
        wrong rather than the code — say so, and the rule changes.
      </Text>

      <CodeBlock class="mt-8" code={WAIVER} wrap="soft" />

      <blockquote class="mt-16 border-l-2 border-primary pl-6">
        <Text variant="lead" class="max-w-2xl font-display italic">
          Errors should never pass silently. Unless explicitly silenced.
        </Text>
      </blockquote>
    </Section>
  </div>
</Page>
